1
00:01:30,460 --> 00:01:34,920
[AWAKEN]

2
00:01:35,570 --> 00:01:38,030
[Episode 8]

3
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,510
Based on our investigation,

4
00:02:03,510 --> 00:02:07,760
we suspect Inspector Su
of colluding with the Communists.

5
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,630
Why Inspector Su?

6
00:02:16,850 --> 00:02:18,470
It was Inspector Su who proposed

7
00:02:18,470 --> 00:02:20,680
sending Shen Kexi to Renji Hospital.

8
00:02:21,430 --> 00:02:24,430
The Communists had scouted
the hospital in advance.

9
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,750
Taking advantage of the fact

10
00:02:26,750 --> 00:02:28,120
that Examining Rooms No. 1 and 2
were interconnected,

11
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:29,560
one of them disguised himself
as a pregnant woman

12
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:31,150
and entered the examining room.

13
00:02:31,150 --> 00:02:33,010
They then took the doctor hostage

14
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:34,190
and sent someone

15
00:02:34,190 --> 00:02:37,050
to assassinate our men
stationed outside the room.

16
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:38,810
After abducting Shen Kexi,

17
00:02:39,630 --> 00:02:41,230
they used Inspector Su's car

18
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:43,560
to make their escape.

19
00:02:48,150 --> 00:02:50,079
Your analysis makes a lot of sense.

20
00:02:52,079 --> 00:02:54,280
But I proposed sending the suspect
to the hospital

21
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:56,740
only to ease the pressure of
public opinion.

22
00:02:58,030 --> 00:03:00,400
Isn't it rather hasty
to conclude from that alone

23
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:01,710
that I was involved in taking him away?

24
00:03:01,710 --> 00:03:02,710
Besides,

25
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,030
he was abducted right under your nose,

26
00:03:06,030 --> 00:03:06,830
Captain Cang.

27
00:03:07,710 --> 00:03:08,510
That's right.

28
00:03:09,470 --> 00:03:11,560
He was taken right from under your nose.

29
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:12,910
Why are you trying to shift the blame

30
00:03:12,910 --> 00:03:14,080
onto Inspector Su?

31
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:18,520
Regardless of whether Inspector Su
is in cahoots with the Communists or not,

32
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:20,050
I'm suspending you for now.

33
00:03:23,750 --> 00:03:25,150
I accept the suspension.

34
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:26,700
But at the same time, I hope

35
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:28,860
Inspector Su can prove her innocence

36
00:03:29,910 --> 00:03:33,070
so that I can accept
this punishment wholeheartedly.

37
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:42,960
General,

38
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:45,240
what's your opinion?

39
00:03:50,870 --> 00:03:53,430
We need Captain Cang's courage—

40
00:03:54,750 --> 00:03:56,680
the courage to question everything.

41
00:03:56,680 --> 00:03:58,240
As long as there are grounds
for suspicion,

42
00:03:58,240 --> 00:04:00,040
no one should be let off the hook.

43
00:04:03,920 --> 00:04:06,960
I think, Inspector Su, you need to

44
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:09,060
explain yourself in this matter.

45
00:04:09,150 --> 00:04:09,750
General.

46
00:04:11,190 --> 00:04:12,630
I suspect someone is

47
00:04:13,250 --> 00:04:15,180
deliberately framing me for this.

48
00:04:15,830 --> 00:04:17,660
Please give me some time, General.

49
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:19,690
I will get to the bottom of this

50
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:22,850
and give you and the Nanjing government
an explanation.

51
00:04:23,630 --> 00:04:25,960
This matter won't be easy to investigate.

52
00:04:26,270 --> 00:04:28,270
It's easier said than done.

53
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:31,120
It could take a year or even longer.

54
00:04:33,740 --> 00:04:35,540
Three days. That's my deadline.

55
00:04:44,270 --> 00:04:44,920
Very well.

56
00:04:46,070 --> 00:04:47,560
Inspector Su, you've got guts.

57
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:49,290
But what if you fail to solve it?

58
00:04:56,390 --> 00:04:58,450
Then I'll go straight back to Nanjing

59
00:05:01,310 --> 00:05:03,770
and submit myself for disciplinary action.

60
00:05:12,870 --> 00:05:15,000
I heard you're on leave.

61
00:05:15,700 --> 00:05:16,950
I'm suspended.

62
00:05:18,070 --> 00:05:18,800
Same thing.

63
00:05:19,630 --> 00:05:20,630
I'm jealous.

64
00:05:26,090 --> 00:05:27,150
Want to get a drink?

65
00:05:41,070 --> 00:05:43,330
Honestly, I was already sick of this job.

66
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:45,659
Getting suspended

67
00:05:45,870 --> 00:05:46,950
suits me just fine.

68
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:50,310
Come on, it's just one prisoner escaping.

69
00:05:50,310 --> 00:05:51,600
We'll find him.

70
00:05:52,470 --> 00:05:55,950
It's not like Director Li's really going
to fire you or something.

71
00:05:55,950 --> 00:05:57,480
If only it were that simple.

72
00:05:59,390 --> 00:06:01,000
If we actually find the guy,

73
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:03,190
he'll be even more furious.

74
00:06:04,010 --> 00:06:04,660
Why?

75
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:08,240
Can't you see it?

76
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:12,370
As long as that Communist isn't found,

77
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:15,740
that woman Su Men will have to
pack her things and go back to Nanjing.

78
00:06:15,740 --> 00:06:16,500
Got it?

79
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:19,610
Now that you put it that way,

80
00:06:19,950 --> 00:06:21,240
this whole thing feels like

81
00:06:21,240 --> 00:06:22,750
a trap for Su Men.

82
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:26,800
Don't talk nonsense.

83
00:06:27,930 --> 00:06:29,050
Well, you said it.

84
00:06:43,430 --> 00:06:45,630
I'm stuck taking the blame for this one.

85
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:49,659
But I've come to terms with it.

86
00:06:50,040 --> 00:06:52,040
As long as I'm alive, that's what matters.

87
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:54,170
Everything else makes no sense at all.

88
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:56,260
You know, you can call that

89
00:06:57,040 --> 00:07:00,230
taking the pressure off Director Li.

90
00:07:05,760 --> 00:07:06,990
Shasha is right.

91
00:07:08,030 --> 00:07:09,560
I'm just his lapdog.

92
00:07:12,070 --> 00:07:15,560
I barely survived the Battle of Nanjing,

93
00:07:16,920 --> 00:07:19,720
and who would've thought
I'd come back to Shanghai

94
00:07:20,750 --> 00:07:23,280
only to live
such a miserable, stifling life?

95
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:28,510
Since when

96
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,530
did I have a nephew like you?

97
00:07:33,390 --> 00:07:34,850
Please forgive me, Uncle.

98
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,330
I'm also from Suichang.

99
00:07:36,920 --> 00:07:39,720
Your cousin's daughter, Rou,

100
00:07:40,390 --> 00:07:41,390
is my girlfriend.

101
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:43,430
Rou?

102
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:45,730
I heard all about you

103
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:47,630
from her.

104
00:07:59,159 --> 00:08:00,360
To tell you the truth,

105
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:03,330
I was captured by the Japanese.

106
00:08:04,050 --> 00:08:06,780
I really had no choice—
I was backed into a corner,

107
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:09,050
s... so I told that lie.

108
00:08:11,750 --> 00:08:13,280
If it was just to stay alive,

109
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:15,230
then telling a harmless lie

110
00:08:15,950 --> 00:08:16,800
was worth it.

111
00:08:18,760 --> 00:08:20,160
I'm from the 3rd Battalion,

112
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:21,890
5th Regiment, 145th Division.

113
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:23,550
Our battalion commander is Du Huangqiao.

114
00:08:23,550 --> 00:08:25,280
I know all the bases of our unit,

115
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:26,800
as well as every one of

116
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,130
our retreat routes.

117
00:08:31,660 --> 00:08:32,460
Sit back down.

118
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:42,299
What do you want in return?

119
00:08:44,270 --> 00:08:45,070
To stay alive.

120
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:47,910
I used to be a man.

121
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:52,550
But now, I'm just a lapdog.

122
00:08:58,270 --> 00:08:59,320
Mr. Zhao.

123
00:09:02,040 --> 00:09:05,110
I've been trying very hard to be a lapdog.

124
00:09:07,550 --> 00:09:08,910
Really hard.

125
00:09:09,240 --> 00:09:10,000
Alright.

126
00:09:10,510 --> 00:09:11,840
Stop thinking about it.

127
00:09:17,910 --> 00:09:18,790
It's gone.

128
00:09:19,140 --> 00:09:20,140
Have a cigarette.

129
00:09:37,750 --> 00:09:39,960
That guy disguised as a pregnant woman
pointed a gun at me and threatened me,

130
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:41,200
telling me not to make a sound.

131
00:09:41,200 --> 00:09:42,270
I was terrified.

132
00:09:42,780 --> 00:09:44,300
Then he asked Nurse Zhang

133
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:46,750
to call the accomplice waiting outside in.

134
00:09:46,750 --> 00:09:47,610
Give me the key.

135
00:09:57,040 --> 00:09:58,550
After Nurse Zhang gave him the key,

136
00:09:58,550 --> 00:09:59,790
they opened this door

137
00:10:00,130 --> 00:10:01,590
and carried that guy away.

138
00:10:04,910 --> 00:10:06,970
Does everyone have a key to this door?

139
00:10:07,270 --> 00:10:09,200
Usually, only the head nurse does.

140
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:13,630
I want to see Nurse Zhang.

141
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:15,600
She didn't come to work today.

142
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:17,530
She was badly shaken up yesterday.

143
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:25,240
Any news?

144
00:10:25,750 --> 00:10:27,320
The nurse's name is Zhang Xiaoyun.

145
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:29,180
She's already applied for leave.

146
00:10:36,560 --> 00:10:37,160
Look.

147
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:39,390
All the keys are

148
00:10:39,750 --> 00:10:40,880
kept here together,

149
00:10:41,670 --> 00:10:42,960
yet Nurse Zhang

150
00:10:42,960 --> 00:10:43,870
just happened to have

151
00:10:43,870 --> 00:10:46,070
the key to Examination Room No. 1 on her.

152
00:10:47,340 --> 00:10:50,470
And the kidnappers somehow
knew exactly that she had it.

153
00:10:51,210 --> 00:10:52,870
You suspect she was involved?

154
00:10:55,250 --> 00:10:56,010
Find her.

155
00:10:56,090 --> 00:10:56,690
Got it.

156
00:11:41,630 --> 00:11:44,190
The bacteria research institute
for Project Slumber

157
00:11:44,190 --> 00:11:46,650
has been secretly established in Shanghai.

158
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:48,760
That's right.

159
00:11:49,920 --> 00:11:51,120
Hoshino's research team

160
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:53,520
has been stationed in Shanghai long-term.

161
00:11:54,670 --> 00:11:57,930
But I didn't expect the Japanese
to take action so quickly.

162
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:01,060
We couldn't decode
the Project Slumber plan

163
00:12:01,490 --> 00:12:02,670
we obtained last time,

164
00:12:02,670 --> 00:12:03,870
and it's useless now.

165
00:12:04,550 --> 00:12:07,320
That's why we're targeting
the research institute this time—

166
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:09,380
to delay them for as long as possible.

167
00:12:11,180 --> 00:12:12,840
What's the specific mission?

168
00:12:13,760 --> 00:12:14,780
Notify the heads of

169
00:12:14,780 --> 00:12:16,960
all 12 stations in the Shanghai District

170
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:18,790
to meet at Fairy Bath in 3 days.

171
00:12:23,390 --> 00:12:24,870
I suspect Su Causeway was deliberately
sent to the hospital

172
00:12:24,870 --> 00:12:25,930
by Cang Guanglian,

173
00:12:26,790 --> 00:12:28,960
and Li Moqun was the one
pulling the strings behind it.

174
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:30,220
You don't understand.

175
00:12:31,210 --> 00:12:33,210
If the director hadn't told me
to be ruthless,

176
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:35,410
would she have ended up in the hospital?

177
00:12:35,540 --> 00:12:37,180
I would've kept that girl

178
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:39,230
in my interrogation room

179
00:12:40,210 --> 00:12:43,490
until she grew into a stone with no mouth.

180
00:12:46,630 --> 00:12:48,670
My visit to Renji Hospital
to check on the injured

181
00:12:48,670 --> 00:12:50,730
had been scheduled several days ago.

182
00:12:51,320 --> 00:12:53,650
So Li Moqun specifically instructed them

183
00:12:53,790 --> 00:12:55,720
to send him to Renji Hospital.

184
00:12:56,390 --> 00:12:57,630
What are you waiting for?

185
00:12:57,630 --> 00:12:58,600
Do as Inspector Su says

186
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:00,100
and send him to Renji Hospital
immediately.

187
00:13:00,100 --> 00:13:00,670
Yes, sir.

188
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:02,200
That old fox.

189
00:13:02,910 --> 00:13:04,200
By having Su Causeway abducted,

190
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:06,340
he not only cemented the suspicion
that he was a Communist,

191
00:13:06,340 --> 00:13:08,200
but also dragged me into the mess.

192
00:13:09,910 --> 00:13:11,510
If we can't find Su Causeway,

193
00:13:11,580 --> 00:13:13,180
he won't let you off the hook.

194
00:13:14,630 --> 00:13:15,590
We must find him.

195
00:13:29,510 --> 00:13:31,440
Are there really 100 pillars here?

196
00:13:32,670 --> 00:13:33,820
I think

197
00:13:34,440 --> 00:13:35,770
there are more than 100.

198
00:13:36,150 --> 00:13:36,790
Let's count again.

199
00:13:36,790 --> 00:13:37,320
Okay.

200
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:39,590
Sister, wait for me.

201
00:13:40,150 --> 00:13:41,150
Eleven, twelve, thirteen...

202
00:13:41,150 --> 00:13:41,870
Sister.

203
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:43,000
Sister.

204
00:13:45,150 --> 00:13:45,790
Sister?

205
00:13:53,510 --> 00:13:54,310
You're awake?

206
00:14:06,030 --> 00:14:07,000
Where am I?

207
00:14:09,790 --> 00:14:11,450
Where you are doesn't matter.

208
00:14:14,790 --> 00:14:17,030
What matters is that you are safe now.

209
00:14:23,870 --> 00:14:24,720
Mr. Guo.

210
00:14:24,790 --> 00:14:27,050
The faucet in your favorite private room

211
00:14:27,150 --> 00:14:28,880
at the very end is broken today.

212
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:30,120
Please switch to a different room for now.

213
00:14:30,120 --> 00:14:31,050
Once it's fixed,

214
00:14:31,110 --> 00:14:33,960
we'll waive the private-room fee
for one day for you.

215
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:34,760
Alright then.

216
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:36,750
Party of one. Please come this way.

217
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:37,840
My apologies.

218
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:43,360
Pedicure for one in Private Room 3.

219
00:14:44,130 --> 00:14:46,390
I should have kicked you all out long ago.

220
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:49,150
Sorry for troubling you, Auntie.

221
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:50,800
Where's Du the Blind?

222
00:14:51,320 --> 00:14:52,320
The patient's awake.

223
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:53,200
He's inside.

224
00:14:55,360 --> 00:14:56,560
She's finally awake.

225
00:14:57,030 --> 00:14:58,120
Tell her to get out of here
as soon as she can walk.

226
00:14:58,120 --> 00:14:58,790
Sure.

227
00:14:59,280 --> 00:15:00,040
Definitely.

228
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:21,410
Who can come pick you up?

229
00:15:21,510 --> 00:15:23,510
I'll help you get in touch with them.

230
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:28,180
I haven't been in contact with my family
for a long time.

231
00:15:29,340 --> 00:15:30,740
In my current condition,

232
00:15:31,440 --> 00:15:33,040
I don't want to trouble them.

233
00:15:35,240 --> 00:15:36,600
Don't play dumb with me.

234
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:39,720
You know I'm not talking about
your family.

235
00:15:41,990 --> 00:15:42,590
Kailai.

236
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:44,320
She's your cousin.

237
00:15:44,670 --> 00:15:45,530
You talk to her.

238
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:50,990
He wants to wait
until you're feeling better

239
00:15:50,990 --> 00:15:52,790
and then get you out of Shanghai.

240
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:58,130
Why do I have to leave Shanghai?

241
00:15:58,670 --> 00:16:00,270
He said you've been exposed.

242
00:16:00,380 --> 00:16:01,210
Exposed how?

243
00:16:05,950 --> 00:16:07,830
No. 76 said I'm a Communist.

244
00:16:09,550 --> 00:16:11,210
Are you saying the same thing?

245
00:16:17,620 --> 00:16:19,020
It's good to be vigilant.

246
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:22,470
Kailai and I have known each other
for a long time.

247
00:16:22,470 --> 00:16:24,150
As for whether I can be trusted,

248
00:16:24,150 --> 00:16:25,150
you can ask him.

249
00:16:29,290 --> 00:16:29,840
Sister.

250
00:16:31,550 --> 00:16:33,630
It was Mr. Du who rescued you.

251
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:36,120
He's a Communist.

252
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:37,440
You can trust him.

253
00:16:39,750 --> 00:16:41,240
But I'm not.

254
00:16:47,630 --> 00:16:49,960
You're the first Communist I've ever met.

255
00:16:56,870 --> 00:16:59,070
Kailai has already told me everything.

256
00:17:03,750 --> 00:17:04,720
Told you what?

257
00:17:15,030 --> 00:17:16,230
I told you so.

258
00:17:16,680 --> 00:17:18,280
My cousin's not a Communist.

259
00:17:18,829 --> 00:17:20,790
No. 76 always frames people for no reason.

260
00:17:20,790 --> 00:17:22,280
I was framed before too.

261
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:28,200
Mr. Du.

262
00:17:30,240 --> 00:17:31,970
Thank you so much for saving me.

263
00:17:33,550 --> 00:17:36,350
But I really just came to Shanghai
to make a living.

264
00:17:40,280 --> 00:17:42,280
Even if I'm not a Communist,

265
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:46,170
there's no way to clear my name now.

266
00:17:46,680 --> 00:17:48,140
Even if I hadn't saved you,

267
00:17:48,200 --> 00:17:49,930
they wouldn't have let you off.

268
00:17:53,190 --> 00:17:54,790
They don't listen to reason.

269
00:17:59,270 --> 00:17:59,880
Miss,

270
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:03,160
what are your plans from here on out?

271
00:18:05,590 --> 00:18:07,110
I don't know what to do,

272
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:11,490
and I have nowhere to go.

273
00:18:17,220 --> 00:18:18,790
Thank you for taking me in.

274
00:18:25,310 --> 00:18:26,970
Whatever your true identity,

275
00:18:27,350 --> 00:18:29,080
you've been targeted by No. 76.

276
00:18:29,240 --> 00:18:31,240
You can't stay in Shanghai anymore.

277
00:18:31,550 --> 00:18:33,610
You need to leave as soon as possible.

278
00:18:34,270 --> 00:18:35,920
But in my current state,

279
00:18:37,370 --> 00:18:38,700
where can I possibly go?

280
00:18:40,750 --> 00:18:42,590
I know of a secret route

281
00:18:42,750 --> 00:18:44,640
that goes from Shanghai
to southern Jiangsu,

282
00:18:44,640 --> 00:18:46,680
and then from southern Jiangsu to Yan'an.

283
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:47,940
Once you get to Yan'an,

284
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:50,820
someone will take care of you
until you recover.

285
00:18:51,510 --> 00:18:52,310
To Yan'an?

286
00:19:19,790 --> 00:19:20,920
When's she leaving?

287
00:19:25,070 --> 00:19:26,330
As soon as she can walk.

288
00:19:26,350 --> 00:19:27,440
I can't wait that long.

289
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:29,570
Get her out of here as soon as possible.

290
00:19:32,270 --> 00:19:33,750
We haven't found her contact yet.

291
00:19:33,750 --> 00:19:34,950
That's your problem.

292
00:19:35,110 --> 00:19:36,970
I've got my own plans to deal with.

293
00:19:39,750 --> 00:19:40,590
What plans?

294
00:19:41,920 --> 00:19:42,850
Let me hear them.

295
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:45,270
Maybe I can help.

296
00:19:46,510 --> 00:19:47,960
Don't think that just because
I helped you hide someone,

297
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:49,760
we're suddenly on the same side.

298
00:19:50,960 --> 00:19:52,490
You're hiding a Communist.

299
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:54,480
If No. 76 or the NBIS finds out,

300
00:19:54,480 --> 00:19:56,340
we'll both be in serious trouble.

301
00:19:58,720 --> 00:20:00,300
You really think after all this commotion,

302
00:20:00,300 --> 00:20:02,360
no one's going to trace it back to you?

303
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:07,140
She's not the only one who needs to leave.

304
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:12,340
You should leave with her.

305
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:23,310
Your fried tofu is really amazing.

306
00:20:24,310 --> 00:20:25,680
I'm worried that if I leave,

307
00:20:25,680 --> 00:20:27,340
I'll never get to eat it again.

308
00:20:28,270 --> 00:20:30,110
I'm talking about something serious here.

309
00:20:30,110 --> 00:20:32,110
Can you please take this seriously?

310
00:20:35,680 --> 00:20:36,960
I think your Fairy Bath

311
00:20:36,960 --> 00:20:38,760
is the safest place in Shanghai.

312
00:20:39,420 --> 00:20:40,750
I'm absolutely certain

313
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:42,530
that you'd never betray me.

314
00:20:43,230 --> 00:20:44,680
And I'd never betray you, either.

315
00:20:44,680 --> 00:20:45,440
Besides,

316
00:20:45,900 --> 00:20:47,250
we have a shared future.

317
00:20:52,640 --> 00:20:53,840
I don't have a future.

318
00:20:57,160 --> 00:20:59,760
Sooner or later, I'm going to die
for the cause.

319
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:05,850
Everyone dies eventually.

320
00:21:09,350 --> 00:21:11,810
That's why what you live for
is what matters.

321
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:15,270
Years ago,

322
00:21:15,550 --> 00:21:17,680
my whole family was killed in Nanjing.

323
00:21:20,790 --> 00:21:23,590
Truth is, I stopped wanting to live
a long time ago.

324
00:21:24,030 --> 00:21:26,110
But now, for a bite of your fried tofu,

325
00:21:27,350 --> 00:21:29,550
I think I can hold on
for a few more years.

326
00:21:32,350 --> 00:21:33,510
It tastes like home.

327
00:21:36,750 --> 00:21:37,920
You're my family.

328
00:21:49,640 --> 00:21:51,700
I haven't had a family for a long time.

329
00:21:52,640 --> 00:21:55,030
Take me home!

330
00:21:57,440 --> 00:22:00,920
Dad, take me home!

331
00:22:01,640 --> 00:22:02,920
Dad!

332
00:22:14,350 --> 00:22:15,410
Between you and me,

333
00:22:15,960 --> 00:22:17,290
politics don't matter.

334
00:22:18,590 --> 00:22:19,920
No matter what happens,

335
00:22:20,680 --> 00:22:24,400
I, Du Huangqiao, will keep you,
Yang Xiaoxian, safe.

336
00:22:26,240 --> 00:22:29,240
Right now, it's not you, Du Huangqiao,
protecting me.

337
00:22:29,350 --> 00:22:30,750
It's me protecting you—

338
00:22:31,030 --> 00:22:32,490
and that comrade of yours.

339
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:34,200
I know, I know.

340
00:22:34,470 --> 00:22:36,270
I won't trouble you for too long.

341
00:22:36,420 --> 00:22:39,110
I'll arrange for her to leave
as soon as possible.

342
00:22:39,110 --> 00:22:39,830
Three days.

343
00:22:42,030 --> 00:22:43,160
No longer than that.

344
00:22:43,830 --> 00:22:45,030
Three days is enough.

345
00:22:49,720 --> 00:22:50,510
Get 2 bowls.

346
00:22:52,160 --> 00:22:53,360
You're in luck today.

347
00:22:53,400 --> 00:22:55,480
I happened to bring back
an extra portion of wontons.

348
00:22:55,480 --> 00:22:56,340
I'm not eating.

349
00:22:57,440 --> 00:22:59,800
Is it just because
I didn't help you save your cousin?

350
00:22:59,800 --> 00:23:01,600
Do you have to ignore me for days?

351
00:23:03,480 --> 00:23:05,530
You had your reasons for not helping.

352
00:23:05,530 --> 00:23:07,480
You're putting on that carefree act

353
00:23:07,480 --> 00:23:08,940
just to piss me off, right?

354
00:23:09,240 --> 00:23:10,300
I'm not that bored.

355
00:23:12,960 --> 00:23:14,420
You're always running off somewhere.

356
00:23:14,420 --> 00:23:16,080
I never know what you're up to.

357
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:18,750
I'm handing over every penny of my salary

358
00:23:18,750 --> 00:23:20,110
from Inspector Su to you.

359
00:23:20,110 --> 00:23:20,880
Happy now?

360
00:23:21,830 --> 00:23:23,440
Then come with me to pick out a cheongsam.

361
00:23:23,440 --> 00:23:24,240
I'm not going.

362
00:23:24,590 --> 00:23:26,850
Su Men hasn't come looking for you today.

363
00:23:27,160 --> 00:23:29,350
Well, that doesn't mean
I have to waste my time with you.

364
00:23:29,350 --> 00:23:31,550
Spending time with me is a waste of time?

365
00:23:44,270 --> 00:23:45,310
Enjoying it, huh?

366
00:24:07,550 --> 00:24:08,400
Don't worry.

367
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:11,070
Other than telling people
you're my cousin,

368
00:24:11,070 --> 00:24:13,070
I haven't said a word to anyone else.

369
00:24:21,550 --> 00:24:22,920
You don't trust Du?

370
00:24:26,980 --> 00:24:28,640
He certainly is very capable.

371
00:24:31,720 --> 00:24:33,580
You really admire him, don't you?

372
00:24:40,550 --> 00:24:42,000
Before Nanjing fell,

373
00:24:43,030 --> 00:24:44,630
I saw him on the battlefield.

374
00:24:46,160 --> 00:24:48,560
He was a Nationalist battalion commander.

375
00:24:49,110 --> 00:24:50,910
Even under such disadvantages,

376
00:24:51,790 --> 00:24:53,720
he insisted on
leading his remaining troops

377
00:24:53,720 --> 00:24:56,450
in a desperate resistance
against the Japanese.

378
00:24:56,790 --> 00:24:57,550
He said

379
00:24:58,750 --> 00:25:00,480
he wanted to save this country.

380
00:25:01,840 --> 00:25:03,530
The Nationalist Party had deceived him,

381
00:25:03,530 --> 00:25:04,790
so he joined your side.

382
00:25:06,140 --> 00:25:07,600
If that's really the case,

383
00:25:08,920 --> 00:25:11,180
then he certainly deserves our respect.

384
00:25:13,880 --> 00:25:15,410
But we have our discipline.

385
00:25:17,070 --> 00:25:18,550
Even if he's one of us,

386
00:25:19,160 --> 00:25:21,360
we cannot reveal our identities to him.

387
00:25:21,400 --> 00:25:22,550
That's our principle.

388
00:25:22,550 --> 00:25:23,310
Got it?

389
00:25:23,470 --> 00:25:24,080
Got it.

390
00:25:28,930 --> 00:25:30,340
If he really is one of us,

391
00:25:32,510 --> 00:25:35,570
then it's right to get me out of here
as soon as possible.

392
00:25:35,860 --> 00:25:36,570
Why?

393
00:25:39,920 --> 00:25:41,110
I have a feeling

394
00:25:42,920 --> 00:25:44,750
that this place isn't nearly as safe

395
00:25:44,750 --> 00:25:45,950
as Du Huangqiao says.

396
00:25:47,240 --> 00:25:48,370
Quite the opposite—

397
00:25:50,440 --> 00:25:51,680
we need to be wary of

398
00:25:51,700 --> 00:25:52,700
everyone here.

399
00:25:59,070 --> 00:26:00,200
"Fragrant Lotus."

400
00:26:06,070 --> 00:26:11,680
♪ Clear waters stir in the cool breeze ♪

401
00:26:17,070 --> 00:26:22,270
♪ Waters stir in the cool breeze ♪

402
00:26:24,350 --> 00:26:28,070
♪ Summer lingers long ♪

403
00:26:37,160 --> 00:26:39,720
♪ Long days linger in summer ♪

404
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:01,240
It's that dangerous?

405
00:27:02,620 --> 00:27:03,950
Then I must find a way

406
00:27:04,240 --> 00:27:06,240
to send you away as soon as possible.

407
00:27:06,680 --> 00:27:07,790
In my current condition,

408
00:27:07,790 --> 00:27:09,120
I can't leave right now.

409
00:27:10,880 --> 00:27:12,550
I can pass a message for you

410
00:27:13,070 --> 00:27:14,930
and have your people come get you.

411
00:27:18,810 --> 00:27:19,870
You don't trust me?

412
00:27:21,310 --> 00:27:22,550
Of course I trust you.

413
00:27:24,400 --> 00:27:27,330
I just can't be sure
what kind of situation you're in.

414
00:27:27,590 --> 00:27:29,250
What if you are being watched?

415
00:27:32,310 --> 00:27:33,590
Doing nothing for now

416
00:27:33,700 --> 00:27:35,830
is actually the safest thing we can do.

417
00:27:38,030 --> 00:27:39,890
But I want to do something for you.

418
00:27:42,960 --> 00:27:45,090
Then chat with me about our childhood.

419
00:27:47,510 --> 00:27:50,960
Do you still remember the Qianzhu House
in Sizhai Village?

420
00:27:53,070 --> 00:27:57,070
And the roasted pigeons
under the big banyan tree.

421
00:28:01,910 --> 00:28:03,020
Thinking back now,

422
00:28:04,920 --> 00:28:06,580
those were truly happy times.

423
00:28:14,960 --> 00:28:15,680
Auntie.

424
00:28:16,030 --> 00:28:16,640
Look.

425
00:28:17,350 --> 00:28:18,280
She drank it all?

426
00:28:19,070 --> 00:28:20,750
Her appetite is getting better every day.

427
00:28:20,750 --> 00:28:22,310
You can rest assured now.

428
00:28:22,830 --> 00:28:24,480
You helped me before,

429
00:28:24,790 --> 00:28:26,650
and now you're helping my cousin.

430
00:28:26,750 --> 00:28:28,200
Auntie, I really don't know

431
00:28:28,200 --> 00:28:29,730
how to repay your kindness.

432
00:28:30,720 --> 00:28:32,200
I'm not much of a person,

433
00:28:32,310 --> 00:28:34,480
but I can tell right from wrong.

434
00:28:34,880 --> 00:28:36,160
It's just a bowl of porridge.

435
00:28:36,160 --> 00:28:37,690
Fairy Bath can afford that.

436
00:28:38,970 --> 00:28:40,920
She needs nourishment right now.

437
00:28:41,270 --> 00:28:41,830
Here,

438
00:28:41,900 --> 00:28:43,200
you watch the bathhouse for me.

439
00:28:43,200 --> 00:28:45,350
I'll go get a pigeon
and stew some soup for her.

440
00:28:45,350 --> 00:28:46,720
No, no, no. I'll go.

441
00:28:47,240 --> 00:28:48,880
You've already done
more than enough for me.

442
00:28:48,880 --> 00:28:50,780
I can't let you spend any more money.

443
00:28:50,780 --> 00:28:52,410
Hold on, hold on. Come here.

444
00:28:54,830 --> 00:28:57,230
You don't have to
stand on ceremony with me.

445
00:28:58,000 --> 00:28:59,750
I originally knitted this for myself,

446
00:28:59,750 --> 00:29:00,870
but the color was too dark.

447
00:29:00,870 --> 00:29:01,650
Lucky you. You can have it.

448
00:29:01,650 --> 00:29:02,440
Try it on.

449
00:29:10,440 --> 00:29:11,440
It's really warm.

450
00:29:12,640 --> 00:29:13,720
The wind in Shanghai

451
00:29:13,720 --> 00:29:14,640
is like a knife.

452
00:29:14,800 --> 00:29:16,610
It could cut your neck clean open.

453
00:29:16,610 --> 00:29:17,310
I have to say,

454
00:29:17,310 --> 00:29:18,840
it looks really good on you.

455
00:29:21,270 --> 00:29:22,230
I don't believe

456
00:29:22,510 --> 00:29:24,240
the wind back in your hometown, Yangzhou,

457
00:29:24,240 --> 00:29:26,510
is soft and gentle all year round.

458
00:29:26,750 --> 00:29:29,080
That's exactly
why I didn't give it to you.

459
00:29:29,790 --> 00:29:31,070
But you,

460
00:29:31,190 --> 00:29:32,750
with that thick skin of yours,

461
00:29:32,750 --> 00:29:34,550
even the wind couldn't cut your neck open.

462
00:29:34,550 --> 00:29:36,310
How come you're so popular

463
00:29:37,030 --> 00:29:39,350
with the ladies?

464
00:29:40,310 --> 00:29:42,830
Auntie, from now on,
your birthday photo shoots

465
00:29:42,830 --> 00:29:43,550
are on me.

466
00:29:43,840 --> 00:29:44,600
For free.

467
00:29:47,680 --> 00:29:49,470
He can take photos for me.

468
00:29:50,880 --> 00:29:52,070
What can you do?

469
00:29:55,750 --> 00:29:56,960
I can marry you.

470
00:29:57,640 --> 00:29:59,000
In your dreams.

471
00:30:24,400 --> 00:30:25,200
Let's go.

472
00:30:25,920 --> 00:30:26,590
Thank you.

473
00:30:26,590 --> 00:30:27,520
You're welcome.

474
00:30:27,880 --> 00:30:28,470
Let's go.

475
00:30:34,400 --> 00:30:36,030
You're back, Nurse Zhang.

476
00:30:43,880 --> 00:30:46,210
You know why I came looking for you,
right?

477
00:30:47,050 --> 00:30:48,770
I don't.

478
00:30:50,480 --> 00:30:53,480
You wouldn't have tried to run away
if you didn't know.

479
00:30:54,640 --> 00:30:56,640
I thought you were debt collectors.

480
00:30:58,190 --> 00:30:59,450
Who do you owe money to?

481
00:31:01,200 --> 00:31:01,880
The casino.

482
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:06,060
You like to gamble?

483
00:31:08,090 --> 00:31:08,680
I...

484
00:31:09,480 --> 00:31:10,810
My husband is a gambler.

485
00:31:11,630 --> 00:31:13,090
He owed money and ran away.

486
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:18,330
How much did they pay you

487
00:31:19,070 --> 00:31:20,030
to open the door?

488
00:31:20,920 --> 00:31:21,510
What?

489
00:31:36,070 --> 00:31:37,200
You opened the door.

490
00:31:37,230 --> 00:31:38,270
I was threatened.

491
00:31:38,920 --> 00:31:40,390
Dr. Zhou can testify for me.

492
00:31:40,390 --> 00:31:42,320
We were all threatened at the time.

493
00:31:43,270 --> 00:31:43,870
Of course.

494
00:31:44,640 --> 00:31:46,370
They must have threatened you.

495
00:31:47,880 --> 00:31:49,070
But how did they know

496
00:31:49,680 --> 00:31:50,720
you had the key?

497
00:31:51,750 --> 00:31:52,960
I have no idea.

498
00:31:56,440 --> 00:31:58,570
I won't make things difficult for you.

499
00:31:58,580 --> 00:32:01,180
And please don't make things
difficult for me.

500
00:32:01,600 --> 00:32:03,160
If I take you back to No. 76,

501
00:32:03,920 --> 00:32:05,550
you'll inevitably suffer.

502
00:32:05,640 --> 00:32:07,200
You won't be able to bear it.

503
00:32:07,640 --> 00:32:09,300
You'll end up talking anyway.

504
00:32:09,640 --> 00:32:10,480
Why bother?

505
00:32:11,790 --> 00:32:13,750
I... I really was forced.

506
00:32:15,210 --> 00:32:16,210
That morning,

507
00:32:16,960 --> 00:32:19,620
the one disguised as a pregnant woman
came to me.

508
00:32:22,070 --> 00:32:23,200
You knew each other?

509
00:32:23,200 --> 00:32:24,160
No, we didn't.

510
00:32:25,720 --> 00:32:28,790
I... To pay off my debts,

511
00:32:29,160 --> 00:32:31,560
I had helped him get penicillin
a few times.

512
00:32:33,000 --> 00:32:34,270
He came to me that day,

513
00:32:34,640 --> 00:32:37,440
saying a woman would be sent to
the emergency room,

514
00:32:37,920 --> 00:32:39,920
and asked me to open the door for him.

515
00:32:40,640 --> 00:32:41,640
Who is he?

516
00:32:42,590 --> 00:32:43,790
I don't know.

517
00:32:50,060 --> 00:32:52,240
You fear they'll retaliate against you?

518
00:32:52,240 --> 00:32:52,920
Yes.

519
00:32:54,450 --> 00:32:56,310
So you dare not tell me, is that it?

520
00:33:02,240 --> 00:33:03,900
Do... Do you have a cigarette?

521
00:33:29,840 --> 00:33:30,800
At first,

522
00:33:31,500 --> 00:33:33,540
the casino sent that guy to me

523
00:33:35,960 --> 00:33:38,160
to help me ease the pressure of my debts.

524
00:33:38,750 --> 00:33:41,270
The force behind the casino
is the Green Gang.

525
00:33:41,270 --> 00:33:43,240
Is that guy also from the Green Gang?

526
00:33:43,240 --> 00:33:44,350
I'm not sure.

527
00:33:44,920 --> 00:33:47,450
Either way, I couldn't afford to
offend them.

528
00:33:49,160 --> 00:33:50,420
What does he look like?

529
00:33:51,480 --> 00:33:52,160
Thin,

530
00:33:53,880 --> 00:33:54,550
tall,

531
00:33:56,680 --> 00:33:57,740
and square-faced.

532
00:33:57,890 --> 00:33:58,750
Anything else?

533
00:34:00,310 --> 00:34:01,920
I want to see Mom.

534
00:34:07,340 --> 00:34:08,380
Be good.

535
00:34:09,090 --> 00:34:09,969
Don't cry.

536
00:34:13,670 --> 00:34:16,510
His pinky finger is

537
00:34:17,670 --> 00:34:18,710
made of metal.

538
00:34:19,280 --> 00:34:20,110
On which hand?

539
00:34:22,630 --> 00:34:23,440
The left hand.

540
00:34:29,070 --> 00:34:30,730
What happened to your finger?

541
00:34:33,550 --> 00:34:34,590
When I was a kid,

542
00:34:35,110 --> 00:34:37,000
I saw my dad working in the field.

543
00:34:37,360 --> 00:34:38,400
I wanted to help,

544
00:34:39,320 --> 00:34:41,380
but I ended up getting cut by a sickle.

545
00:34:41,489 --> 00:34:42,750
His name is Ding Awang,

546
00:34:42,780 --> 00:34:44,310
a pedicurist at Fairy Bath.

547
00:34:45,850 --> 00:34:47,110
It's Fairy Bath again.

548
00:34:47,670 --> 00:34:49,130
I'll go check it out first.

549
00:34:50,360 --> 00:34:52,620
Then I'll go investigate the Green Gang.

550
00:34:53,080 --> 00:34:53,679
Good luck.

551
00:34:55,710 --> 00:34:56,389
You too.

552
00:35:17,550 --> 00:35:19,210
It's pretty quiet here today.

553
00:35:19,230 --> 00:35:21,070
Mr. Zhao, look at the time.

554
00:35:21,070 --> 00:35:22,400
You came after closing.

555
00:35:22,480 --> 00:35:23,230
What?

556
00:35:23,590 --> 00:35:24,960
Not receiving customers anymore?

557
00:35:24,960 --> 00:35:26,760
I wouldn't receive anyone else,

558
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:28,440
but you're an exception.

559
00:35:30,480 --> 00:35:31,360
The usual?

560
00:35:33,000 --> 00:35:34,200
I'll just take a bath.

561
00:35:35,440 --> 00:35:37,360
Mr. Zhao, you're here so late.

562
00:35:37,360 --> 00:35:38,230
Been busy all day.

563
00:35:38,230 --> 00:35:39,030
Need a pedicure?

564
00:35:39,030 --> 00:35:40,690
I'm tired. Just a bath will do.

565
00:35:40,760 --> 00:35:41,890
Thank you, Mr. Zhao.

566
00:35:42,320 --> 00:35:44,850
I was wondering
why it was so quiet here today.

567
00:35:45,070 --> 00:35:47,190
Turns out we're missing
Master Du's three-stringed instrument.

568
00:35:47,190 --> 00:35:48,260
There aren't many customers today,

569
00:35:48,260 --> 00:35:49,860
so he's taking the night off.

570
00:35:51,760 --> 00:35:52,630
I'll go in then.

571
00:35:53,110 --> 00:35:54,370
Please take your time.

572
00:38:24,760 --> 00:38:25,550
Mr. Zhao.

573
00:38:26,070 --> 00:38:27,000
Why are you here?

574
00:38:27,670 --> 00:38:29,280
Is it strange for me to be here?

575
00:38:29,280 --> 00:38:31,670
Shouldn't you be at the dance hall
at this hour?

576
00:38:31,670 --> 00:38:34,070
I'm tired today.
Just wanted to take a bath.

577
00:38:34,440 --> 00:38:35,550
It's still quite warm.

578
00:38:35,550 --> 00:38:36,360
Who is it for?

579
00:38:38,110 --> 00:38:40,280
Xiaoxian wanted to have some chestnuts.

580
00:38:40,280 --> 00:38:42,120
I looked around but couldn't find her.

581
00:38:42,120 --> 00:38:44,520
It's cold.
It's good to eat something warm.

582
00:38:44,630 --> 00:38:45,510
Have a taste.

583
00:38:47,400 --> 00:38:48,000
Here.

584
00:38:48,760 --> 00:38:49,840
Why are your hands so cold?

585
00:38:49,840 --> 00:38:51,030
It's freezing outside.

586
00:38:51,030 --> 00:38:52,510
The wind cuts like a knife.

587
00:38:54,690 --> 00:38:57,070
But Mr. Chen, you've got someone
looking out for you.

588
00:38:57,070 --> 00:38:58,800
Who knitted that scarf for you?

589
00:38:59,400 --> 00:39:00,510
Xiaoxian.

590
00:39:00,630 --> 00:39:03,090
That's why I bought chestnuts
to please her.

591
00:39:03,320 --> 00:39:04,840
You two really are close.

592
00:39:05,590 --> 00:39:07,880
Maybe I'll have someone knit me one too.

593
00:39:09,720 --> 00:39:12,590
If you really want one, you could
have enough to open a whole shop.

594
00:39:12,590 --> 00:39:13,070
See you.

595
00:39:13,070 --> 00:39:13,600
Alright.

596
00:39:32,360 --> 00:39:34,150
Mr. Zhao, finished your bath?

597
00:39:34,360 --> 00:39:35,620
I really am a nuisance,

598
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:37,710
coming in and disturbing you
right at closing time.

599
00:39:37,710 --> 00:39:38,630
Not at all.

600
00:39:41,610 --> 00:39:42,120
I'm off.

601
00:39:42,670 --> 00:39:43,400
Take care.

602
00:40:06,030 --> 00:40:07,350
I just went looking for you.

603
00:40:07,350 --> 00:40:08,160
I knocked, but no one answered.

604
00:40:08,160 --> 00:40:10,090
He didn't notice anything, did he?

605
00:40:12,800 --> 00:40:14,600
He was in the bath the whole time.

606
00:40:15,480 --> 00:40:17,510
Living on tenterhooks like this every day.

607
00:40:17,510 --> 00:40:18,990
If No. 76 finds out,

608
00:40:19,350 --> 00:40:21,150
none of us will make it out alive.

609
00:40:22,320 --> 00:40:23,710
I left the front door open for you,

610
00:40:23,710 --> 00:40:25,970
but Mr. Zhao, you prefer climbing walls.

611
00:40:26,190 --> 00:40:27,440
There are prying eyes everywhere.

612
00:40:27,440 --> 00:40:28,770
Better safe than sorry.

613
00:40:32,710 --> 00:40:34,230
She should be in the special care room

614
00:40:34,230 --> 00:40:35,030
at Fairy Bath.

615
00:40:38,670 --> 00:40:39,440
Are you sure?

616
00:40:40,870 --> 00:40:42,870
I think Chen Kailai's involved too.

617
00:40:43,160 --> 00:40:45,290
You want me to go make contact with him?

618
00:40:48,390 --> 00:40:49,870
Chen Kailai is very smart,

619
00:40:50,630 --> 00:40:53,090
and his actions so far
have earned our trust.

620
00:40:55,000 --> 00:40:56,460
But have you ever wondered

621
00:40:57,800 --> 00:41:00,600
why Shen Kexi didn't have him
deliver the message?

622
00:41:05,540 --> 00:41:07,400
Chen Kailai hasn't been trained,

623
00:41:07,960 --> 00:41:09,790
and the situation around him is unclear.

624
00:41:09,790 --> 00:41:11,590
She was worried he'd be exposed.

625
00:41:14,930 --> 00:41:15,810
In my opinion,

626
00:41:16,020 --> 00:41:17,420
it's not just Ding Awang—

627
00:41:18,150 --> 00:41:21,210
the whole situation at Fairy Bath
is very complicated.

628
00:41:22,020 --> 00:41:24,110
I was wondering why Boss Yang
hasn't been moving around much.

629
00:41:24,110 --> 00:41:25,040
Are you injured?

630
00:41:25,710 --> 00:41:28,170
After the assassination at the racecourse,

631
00:41:28,320 --> 00:41:29,480
Boss Yang

632
00:41:30,110 --> 00:41:31,640
suddenly started limping.

633
00:41:33,400 --> 00:41:34,530
She's with the NBIS?

634
00:41:37,280 --> 00:41:39,150
And that master
who plays the three-stringed instrument,

635
00:41:39,150 --> 00:41:40,070
Du Huangqiao,

636
00:41:43,150 --> 00:41:44,350
isn't simple either.

637
00:41:50,890 --> 00:41:53,110
Just like the mist that won't clear
in that bathhouse—

638
00:41:53,110 --> 00:41:55,070
everyone's a mystery,

639
00:41:56,390 --> 00:41:58,450
as if everyone has another identity.

640
00:42:01,360 --> 00:42:02,800
In this case,

641
00:42:03,520 --> 00:42:06,120
we definitely can't rush into
making contact.

642
00:42:07,190 --> 00:42:09,250
I left a code message for Su Causeway.

643
00:42:09,830 --> 00:42:11,430
If she really is in there,

644
00:42:12,480 --> 00:42:13,320
she'll know

645
00:42:14,880 --> 00:42:16,080
that we've found her.

646
00:42:23,840 --> 00:42:25,100
Your scarf looks nice.

647
00:42:28,150 --> 00:42:29,280
I knitted it myself.

648
00:42:30,320 --> 00:42:32,520
Maybe I'll have someone knit me one too.

649
00:42:33,510 --> 00:42:34,400
If you like it,

650
00:42:35,150 --> 00:42:36,590
I can knit one for you too.

651
00:42:38,060 --> 00:42:39,660
Hello, Comrade Su Causeway.

652
00:42:39,750 --> 00:42:40,680
Nice to meet you.

653
00:42:45,550 --> 00:42:47,480
You two really are on the same page.

654
00:42:50,770 --> 00:42:52,690
Now we have to figure out a way

655
00:42:52,840 --> 00:42:54,400
to get her out of Fairy Bath.

656
00:42:57,480 --> 00:43:00,410
We'll have to resort to
the emergency contact method

657
00:43:00,510 --> 00:43:01,840
and leave her a message.

658
00:43:02,880 --> 00:43:04,480
I hope our judgment is correct.
